# PReP's spread ISA ports and direct-mapped PCI configuration, which no page
# mapping can express, emulated: every mapping of them points at a window of
# unclaimed Bandit memory whose pages are mapped no-access, and the
# protection fault an access there takes is decoded and done on the Network
# Server's hardware (src/kernel-trap.c): the VGA ports, PCI configuration
# (the first 53C825A as a 53C810, the 54M30 as a CL-GD5434, memory BARs in
# PReP's numbering), the NVRAM and the 8042 (patch 98).  A Power Macintosh
# without those two cards gets stand-ins in their slots: a 53C810 whose
# registers are MESH's (patch 96), and the on-board Control, whose memory is
# a shadow frame buffer that the clock copies to the screen
# (src/kernel-video.c; patch 57).  The SCSI driver loses PReP's DMA offset
# (src/dd-scsi-dma.S, generated by tools/gen-dma-patch.py).  Needs patches
# 70, 80 and 95.
file /MK/MK_TEST.PPC
asm src/kernel-trap.c 53c494629337
asm src/kernel-video.c 00add9c62415
file /MK/DD_SCSI0.DYN
asm src/dd-scsi-dma.S b05e5e2761cb
file /MK/DD_SCSI1.DYN
asm src/dd-scsi-dma.S b05e5e2761cb
